  "reasoning": "For the 2026 U.S. Senate race, multiple recent polls show Democratic incumbent Jon Ossoff consistently ahead of Republican Mike Collins by mid- to high-single-digit margins: an AARP poll has Ossoff 52%-43%, Emerson 48%-43%, and other coverage cites leads ranging from 4 to 13 points, with Cook Political Report and Sabato rating the race Lean Democratic.[6][13][14][18] In the 2026 gubernatorial race, Democrat Keisha Lance Bottoms holds a small but persistent lead over Republican Rick Jackson in several recent polls: State Navigate finds 51%-44% with leaners, Fox News/FOX 5 reports 52%-47%, and AARP shows 48%-42%, while Cook rates the race a toss-up despite Bottoms\u2019 edge.[5][7][12][14][18] Taken together, these polls indicate Georgia is currently leaning Democratic in high-profile statewide federal contests, though margins are modest and the environment remains competitive, warranting less than maximal confidence.",
